---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Portrait from '../assets/jon-reading.jpeg';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About Jon Kohlmeier · Puffs of Smoke"
  description="About Jon Kohlmeier, a husband, father, Revenue Operations lead, reader, and occasional winemaker in Cedar Rapids, Iowa."
>
  <header class="about-hero container-page">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About Jon</p>
      <h1>A little about me.</h1>
      <p class="page-header__lede">I’m Jon Kohlmeier. I live in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, with my wife and our daughter.</p>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <Image src={Portrait} alt="Jon Kohlmeier reading in his study" width={600} height={600} />
      <figcaption>Jon Kohlmeier · Cedar Rapids, Iowa</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>

  <div class="about-body container-page">
    <aside class="about-body__aside">
      <p class="pull-quote">
        A good friend of mine once told his son, “Jon makes people successful.” I’ve always liked that description. It’s
        probably a better explanation of what I do than my actual job title.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <div class="about-body__content prose prose--page">
      <p>
        I’ve taken a somewhat roundabout path to where I am today. I started out studying theology, discovered that Koine
        Greek and I weren’t getting along, and eventually earned a degree in IT. Along the way, I worked in web
        development, marketing, and a few other roles that didn’t always seem connected at the time.
      </p>
      <p>
        These days I work in Revenue Operations at West Music, a company that’s been helping people make music for more
        than 80 years. My job is a little hard to explain at parties. I spend a lot of time figuring out why things aren’t
        working the way they should, helping people understand one another, and trying to make complicated work a little
        simpler.
      </p>

      <h2>More than work</h2>
      <p>I’ve never been particularly good at having just one interest.</p>
      <p>
        I’m a Lutheran, a husband, a father, an occasional winemaker, and a reader who buys books faster than he finishes
        them. I enjoy a good Manhattan, an old movie, a quiet evening at home, and conversations that wander well beyond
        where they started.
      </p>
      <p>
        I like technology, but I’m increasingly interested in what it does to the people using it. I like thinking about
        leadership, but I’m more interested in what makes someone worth following than what title they hold.
      </p>
      <p>
        And becoming a father has made me think quite a bit about time. Not just how to use it productively, but what
        makes it worth spending in the first place.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Puffs of Smoke?</h2>
      <p>
        I’ve been writing on and off for a long time, usually in fits and starts. Some of it has been about work. Some
        about faith, technology, books, and whatever happened to catch my attention.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a while I thought a personal website needed a particular subject. Something useful enough to build an
        audience around.
      </p>
      <p>I’m less convinced of that now.</p>
      <p>
        Puffs of Smoke is simply a place to write. Some pieces will be thoughtful. Others might be practical,
        opinionated, nostalgic, or just a record of something I enjoyed.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name comes from my fondness for a pipe and the kind of conversations that happen when nobody’s in much of a
        hurry.
      </p>
      <p>
        I don’t expect everything here to fit neatly together. But I hope that, over time, it gives a reasonably honest
        picture of how I see the world.
      </p>
      <p>Thanks for stopping by.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
